  Windows Troubleshooting Documentation


This section contains my hands-on troubleshooting notes while fixing Windows problems.

## Purpose ##
This section documents my hands-on troubleshooting process while working through common Windows problems. 
It serves as both a record of my current knowledge and a reference I can return to when encountering similar issues in the future.
The goal is to track the troubleshooting process, including initial observations, investigation steps, screenshots, and solutions,
while gradually building a personal knowledge base of Windows diagnostics and problem solving.

Each folder contains:
- raw  thought pproccess 
- Structured work through 
- screenshots
- solutions 

